Desar...","fr":"Guide de Mise en Place SCM pour les Flux de Travail de Dé...","de":"SCM-Setup-Leitfaden für Entwicklungsworkflows mit Claude ...","pt":"Guia de Configuração SCM: Melhores Práticas para Controle...","ru":"Настройка SCM: Руководство по лучшим практикам контроля в...","ar":"دليل إعداد SCM: أفضل الممارسات لإدارة الإصدارات للوكلاء ا..."},"description":{"en":"Unlock efficient AI-powered development workflows with scm, featuring Git best practices and conflict resolution techniques - learn how to implement today!","zh":"了解SCM技能，实现Git最佳实践和AI工具集成，提高开发效率","ja":"SCMスキルをマスターし、GitベストプラクティスとAIエージェントを統合して開発効率を向上させる","ko":"SCM 스킬을 익혀 Git 최고의 실천과 AI 툴을 통합하여 개발 효율성을 높여라","es":"Aprende a implementar las mejores prácticas de SCM con Claude Code para mejorar tus flujos de trabajo de desarrollo con Git","fr":"Découvrez comment mettre en place les meilleures pratiques de SCM avec Claude Code pour améliorer vos flux de travail de développement avec Git","de":"Erfahren Sie, wie Sie SCM-Best-Practices mit Claude Code umsetzen, um Ihre Entwicklungsworkflows mit Git zu verbessern","pt":"Aprenda a configurar o SCM com as melhores práticas para controle de versão, incluindo commits atômicos e resolução de conflitos","ru":"Узнайте, как настроить SCM с лучшими практиками контроля версий, включая атомарные коммиты и разрешение конфликтов для ИИ Агентов","ar":"تعرف على كيفية إعداد SCM بأفضل الممارسات لإدارة الإصدارات، بما في ذلك التعهدات الذرية وحل النزاعات للوكلاء الذكيين"},"definition":{"en":"scm is a source control management skill that implements Git best practices and workflows for efficient development and team collaboration","zh":"SCM是源代码管理技能，用于实现Git最佳实践和AI工具集成","ja":"SCMはソースコード管理スキルで、GitベストプラクティスとAIエージェントを統合する","ko":"SCM은 소스 코드 관리 스킬로서 Git 최고의 실천과 AI 툴을 통합하는 것을 의미","es":"El SCM (Source Control Management) es una habilidad que ayuda a los desarrolladores a gestionar cambios en su código con Git","fr":"Le SCM (Source Control Management) est une compétence qui aide les développeurs à gérer les modifications de leur code avec Git","de":"SCM (Source Control Management) ist eine Fähigkeit, die Entwicklern hilft, Änderungen in ihrem Code mit Git zu verwalten","pt":"O que é SCM? É uma habilidade de controle de versão que ajuda equipes de desenvolvimento a gerenciar mudanças no código","ru":"Что такое SCM? Это навык контроля версий, который помогает командам разработки управлять изменениями в коде для ИИ Агентов","ar":"ما هي SCM؟ هي مهارة لإدارة الإصدارات تساعد فرق التطوير في إدارة التغييرات في الكود للوكلاء الذكيين"},"features":{"en":["Enforces atomic commits with one logical change per commit","Implements conventional commits using `type(scope): description` format","Maintains clean history through rebasing before merge","Supports branch naming conventions with `type/ticket-description` format","Facilitates team collaboration through pull requests (PRs) and conflict resolution"],"zh":["Atomic Commits: 一次提交一个逻辑变化","Conventional Commits: 使用type(scope): description格式","Clean History: 合并前重置以保持线性历史","Branch Naming: 使用type/ticket-description格式","PR: 合并请求"],"ja":["Atomic Commits: 1つのコミットに1つの論理的な変更","Conventional Commits: type(scope): description形式を使用","Clean History: マージ前にリベースして線形の履歴を保持","Branch Naming: type/ticket-description形式を使用","PR: プルリクエスト"],"ko":["Atomic Commits: 한 번에 하나의 논리적 변경","Conventional Commits: type(scope): description 형식을 사용","Clean History: 병합 전에 리베이스하여 선형적인 기록을 유지","Branch Naming: type/ticket-description 형식을 사용","PR: 풀 리퀘스트"],"es":["Atomic Commits para cambios lógicos","Conventional Commits con formato `type(scope): description`","Clean History con rebase antes de merge","Branch Naming con formato `type/ticket-description`","PRs para colaboración en equipo"],"fr":["Atomic Commits pour des changements logiques","Conventional Commits avec format `type(scope): description`","Clean History avec rebase avant merge","Branch Naming avec format `type/ticket-description`","PRs pour la collaboration d''équipe"],"de":["Atomic Commits für logische Änderungen","Conventional Commits mit Format `type(scope): description`","Clean History mit Rebase vor Merge","Branch Naming mit Format `type/ticket-description`","PRs für Teamzusammenarbeit"],"pt":["Commits atômicos para mudanças lógicas","Commits convencionais com formato `type(scope): description`","Histórico de commits limpo com rebase antes de merge","Nomeação de branches com formato `type/ticket-description`","Resolução de conflitos e colaboração em equipe"],"ru":["Атомарные коммиты для логических изменений","Конвенциональные коммиты с форматом `type(scope): description`","Чистая история коммитов с ребейзом перед мерджем","Именование веток с форматом `type/ticket-description`","Разрешение конфликтов и командная работа для ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["التعهدات الذرية للتغييرات المنطقية","التعهدات التقليدية بالتنسيق `type(scope): description`","التاريخ النظيف للتغييرات مع إعادة الترتيب قبل الدمج","تسمية الفروع بالتنسيق `type/ticket-description`","حل النزاعات والتعاون الفعلي لفريق التطوير للوكلاء الذكيين"]},"keywords":{"en":["scm setup guide","Git best practices","how to use scm","scm vs gitflow","scm install","what is scm","scm alternative","conflict resolution techniques","AI-powered development workflows"],"zh":["SCM技能","Git最佳实践","AI工具集成","源代码管理","版本控制","Git工作流","代码审查","开发效率","AI开发工具"],"ja":["SCMスキル","Gitベストプラクティス","AIエージェント統合","ソースコード管理","バージョン管理","Gitワークフロー","コードレビュー","開発効率","AI開発ツール"],"ko":["SCM 스킬","Git 최고의 실천","AI 툴 통합","소스 코드 관리","버전 관리","Git 작업 흐름","코드 리뷰","개발 효율성","AI 개발 툴"],"es":["SCM con Claude Code","mejores prácticas de Git","flujos de trabajo de desarrollo","herramientas de desarrollo con AI","AI Agents para desarrollo","desarrollo con Git","colaboración en equipo con Git","gestión de cambios con Git"],"fr":["SCM avec Claude Code","meilleures pratiques de Git","flux de travail de développement","outils de développement avec IA","IA Agents pour développement","développement avec Git","collaboration d''équipe avec Git","gestion de modifications avec Git"],"de":["SCM mit Claude Code","Best-Practices für Git","Entwicklungsworkflows","Entwicklungstools mit KI","KI-Agents für Entwicklung","Entwicklung mit Git","Teamzusammenarbeit mit Git","Änderungsmanagement mit Git"],"pt":["SCM","controle de versão","commits atômicos","commits convencionais","resolução de conflitos","colaboração em equipe","desenvolvimento de software","gerenciamento de código"],"ru":["SCM","контроль версий","атомарные коммиты","конвенциональные коммиты","разрешение конфликтов","командная работа","разработка программного обеспечения","управление кодом","ИИ Агенты"],"ar":["SCM","إدارة الإصدارات","التعهدات الذرية","التعهدات التقليدية","حل النزاعات","التعاون الفعلي","تطوير البرمجيات","إدارة الكود","الوكلاء الذكيين"]}},"owner":"mauromedda","repo":"agent-toolkit","repoPath":"mauromedda/agent-toolkit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.271Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"scm","description":">-","bodyPreview":"# ABOUTME: Source control management skill for Git best practices and workflows\n# ABOUTME: Covers branching, commits, PRs, conflict resolution, and team collaboration\n\n# Source Control Management (SCM) Skill\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Principle | Rule |\n|-----------|------|\n| Atomic Commits | One logical change per commit |\n| Conventional Commits | `type(scope): description` format |\n| Clean History | Rebase before merge for linear history |\n| Branch Naming | `type/ticket-description` format |\n| PR","body":"# ABOUTME: Source control management skill for Git best practices and workflows\n# ABOUTME: Covers branching, commits, PRs, conflict resolution, and team collaboration\n\n# Source Control Management (SCM) Skill\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Principle | Rule |\n|-----------|------|\n| Atomic Commits | One logical change per commit |\n| Conventional Commits | `type(scope): description` format |\n| Clean History | Rebase before merge for linear history |\n| Branch Naming | `type/ticket-description` format |\n| PR Size | < 400 lines of code changes |\n| Never Force Push | To shared branches (main, develop) |\n\n## 🔄 RESUMED SESSION CHECKPOINT\n\n**When a session is resumed from context compaction, verify Git state:**\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  SESSION RESUMED - SCM SKILL VERIFICATION                   │\n│                                                             │\n│  Before continuing Git operations:                          │\n│                                                             │\n│  1. Was I in the middle of Git operations?                  │\n│     → Check summary for \"commit\", \"merge\", \"rebase\"         │\n│                                                             │\n│  2. Current repository state:                               │\n│     → Run: git status                                       │\n│     → Run: git log --oneline -5                             │\n│     → Run: git branch -vv                                   │\n│                                                             │\n│  3. Pending operations:                                     │\n│     → Check for: .git/MERGE_HEAD (merge in progress)        │\n│     → Check for: .git/rebase-merge (rebase in progress)     │\n│     → Check for: .git/CHERRY_PICK_HEAD (cherry-pick)        │\n│                                                             │\n│  If operation was interrupted:                              │\n│  → Complete or abort the pending operation                  │\n│  → Verify working directory is clean                        │\n│  → Ensure no uncommitted changes are lost                   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Branching Strategies\n\n### Git Flow (Traditional)\n\n```\nmain ─────●─────────────────●─────────────●──────\n          │                 ↑             ↑\n          │         merge   │     merge   │\n          ↓                 │             │\ndevelop ──●──●──●──●──●─────●──●──●──●────●──────\n              │     ↑           │     ↑\n              ↓     │           ↓     │\nfeature/xyz ──●──●──┘   feature/abc ──●──┘\n```\n\n**Use when:**\n- Scheduled releases\n- Multiple versions in production\n- Formal QA process\n\n**Branches:**\n- `main`: Production code\n- `develop`: Integration branch\n- `feature/*`: New features\n- `release/*`: Release preparation\n- `hotfix/*`: Emergency fixes\n\n### GitHub Flow (Simplified)\n\n```\nmain ─────●───────●───────●───────●──────\n          │       ↑       │       ↑\n          ↓       │       ↓       │\nfeature ──●──●──●─┘ fix ──●──●────┘\n```\n\n**Use when:**\n- Continuous deployment\n- Small teams\n- Rapid iteration\n\n**Branches:**\n- `main`: Always deployable\n- `feature/*`, `fix/*`, `chore/*`: Short-lived branches\n\n### Trunk-Based Development\n\n```\nmain ─────●──●──●──●──●──●──●──●──●──────\n          ↑     ↑     ↑     ↑     ↑\n          │     │     │     │     │\n          └─────┴─────┴─────┴─────┴── Small, frequent commits\n```\n\n**Use when:**\n- Mature CI/CD pipeline\n- Feature flags available\n- High-trust team\n\n## Branch Naming Convention\n\n```\n<type>/<ticket>-<brief-description>\n\nExamples:\n- feature/PROJ-123-user-authentication\n- fix/PROJ-456-login-timeout\n- chore/PROJ-789-update-dependencies\n- docs/PROJ-012-api-documentation\n- refactor/PROJ-345-extract-service\n```\n\n| Type | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `feature/` | New functionality |\n| `fix/` | Bug fixes |\n| `chore/` | Maintenance tasks |\n| `docs/` | Documentation only |\n| `refactor/` | Code restructuring |\n| `test/` | Test additions |\n| `hotfix/` | Emergency production fixes |\n\n## Conventional Commits\n\n### Format\n\n```\n<type>(<scope>): <description>\n\n[optional body]\n\n[optional footer(s)]\n```\n\n### Types\n\n| Type | Description | Triggers |\n|------|-------------|----------|\n| `feat` | New feature | Minor version bump |\n| `fix` | Bug fix | Patch version bump |\n| `docs` | Documentation only | No version bump |\n| `style` | Formatting, no code change | No version bump |\n| `refactor` | Code change, no feature/fix | No version bump |\n| `test` | Adding/fixing tests | No version bump |\n| `chore` | Build process, tooling | No version bump |\n| `perf` | Performance improvement | Patch version bump |\n| `ci` | CI configuration | No version bump |\n| `build` | Build system changes | No version bump |\n| `revert` | Revert previous commit | Varies |\n\n### Examples\n\n```bash\n# Feature with scope\nfeat(auth): add OAuth2 login support\n\n# Bug fix with body\nfix(api): handle null response from payment gateway\n\nThe payment gateway occasionally returns null instead of\nan error object. Added null check before processing.\n\nFixes #123\n\n# Breaking change\nfeat(api)!: change user endpoint response format\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: The /api/users endpoint now returns\na paginated response object instead of an array.\n\n# Multiple footers\nfix(security): upgrade vulnerable dependency\n\nReviewed-by: John Doe\nRefs: CVE-2024-12345\n```\n\n## Commit Best Practices\n\n### Atomic Commits\n\nEach commit should:\n- Represent ONE logical change\n- Be independently revertable\n- Pass all tests\n- Have a clear, descriptive message\n\n```bash\n# BAD: Multiple unrelated changes\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"various fixes and updates\"\n\n# GOOD: Separate logical changes\ngit add src/auth/\ngit commit -m \"feat(auth): implement password reset flow\"\n\ngit add tests/auth/\ngit commit -m \"test(auth): add password reset tests\"\n\ngit add package.json package-lock.json\ngit commit -m \"chore(deps): update authentication libraries\"\n```\n\n### Interactive Staging\n\n```bash\n# Stage specific hunks\ngit add -p\n\n# Stage specific files interactively\ngit add -i\n```\n\n### Commit Message Guidelines\n\n**Subject line:**\n- Max 50 characters\n- Imperative mood (\"add\" not \"added\")\n- No period at end\n- Capitalize first word after type\n\n**Body (optional):**\n- Wrap at 72 characters\n- Explain WHAT and WHY, not HOW\n- Reference issues/tickets\n\n```bash\n# Use editor for complex commits\ngit commit\n\n# Quick commit with message\ngit commit -m \"fix(api): correct rate limit calculation\"\n```\n\n## Merging vs Rebasing\n\n### When to Merge\n\n```bash\n# Merge preserves history\ngit checkout main\ngit merge feature/user-auth --no-ff\n\n# Creates merge commit:\n# *   Merge branch ''feature/user-auth''\n# |\\\n# | * feat: add login endpoint\n# | * feat: add user model\n# |/\n# *   Previous commit on main\n```\n\n**Use merge when:**\n- Preserving feature branch history is important\n- Working with public/shared branches\n- Team prefers merge commits\n\n### When to Rebase\n\n```bash\n# Rebase creates linear history\ngit checkout feature/user-auth\ngit rebase main\n\n# Results in linear history:\n# * feat: add login endpoint\n# * feat: add user model\n# * Previous commit on main\n```\n\n**Use rebase when:**\n- Cleaning up local commits before PR\n- Updating feature branch with main\n- Maintaining linear project history\n\n### Interactive Rebase for Cleanup\n\n```bash\n# Squash, reorder, edit last 5 commits\ngit rebase -i HEAD~5\n\n# In editor:\npick abc1234 feat: add user model\nsquash def5678 fix: typo in user model\npick ghi9012 feat: add login endpoint\nreword jkl3456 feat: add logout endpoint\ndrop mno7890 WIP: debugging\n\n# Commands:\n# p, pick   = use commit\n# r, reword = use commit but edit message\n# e, edit   = use commit but stop for amending\n# s, squash = meld into previous commit\n# f, fixup  = like squash but discard message\n# d, drop   = remove commit\n```\n\n## Pull Request Workflow\n\n### Before Creating PR\n\n```bash\n# 1. Ensure branch is up to date\ngit fetch origin\ngit rebase origin/main\n\n# 2. Run tests locally\nnpm test  # or equivalent\n\n# 3. Check for linting issues\nnpm run lint  # or equivalent\n\n# 4. Review your changes\ngit diff origin/main...HEAD\ngit log origin/main..HEAD --oneline\n```\n\n### PR Size Guidelines\n\n| Size | Lines Changed | Review Time |\n|------|---------------|-------------|\n| XS | < 50 | Minutes |\n| S | 50-200 | < 30 min |\n| M | 200-400 | < 1 hour |\n| L | 400-800 | Hours |\n| XL | > 800 | Split required |\n\n### PR Description Template\n\n```markdown\n## Summary\nBrief description of changes (1-3 bullet points)\n\n## Changes\n- Added X feature\n- Modified Y component\n- Fixed Z bug\n\n## Testing\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] Integration tests pass\n- [ ] Manual testing completed\n\n## Screenshots (if UI changes)\n[Before/After screenshots]\n\n## Related Issues\nCloses #123\nRefs #456\n```\n\n## Conflict Resolution\n\n### Understanding Conflicts\n\n```\n<<<<<<< HEAD (current branch)\nconst timeout = 5000;\n=======\nconst timeout = 10000;\n>>>>>>> feature-branch (incoming changes)\n```\n\n### Resolution Strategies\n\n```bash\n# 1. Keep current branch version\ngit checkout --ours path/to/file\n\n# 2. Keep incoming version\ngit checkout --theirs path/to/file\n\n# 3. Manual resolution\n# Edit file, then:\ngit add path/to/file\ngit rebase --continue  # or git merge --continue\n```\n\n### Prevention Strategies\n\n- Pull/rebase frequently\n- Keep branches short-lived\n- Communicate about shared files\n- Use code owners for critical paths\n\n## Git Configuration\n\n### Essential Configuration\n\n```bash\n# Identity\ngit config --global user.name \"Your Name\"\ngit config --global user.email \"your.email@example.com\"\n\n# Default branch\ngit config --global init.defaultBranch main\n\n# Editor\ngit config --global core.editor \"code --wait\"\n\n# Diff tool\ngit config --global diff.tool vscode\ngit config --global difftool.vscode.cmd ''code --wait --diff $LOCAL $REMOTE''\n\n# Merge tool\ngit config --global merge.tool vscode\ngit config --global mergetool.vscode.cmd ''code --wait $MERGED''\n\n# Auto-correct typos\ngit config --global help.autocorrect 10\n\n# Prune deleted remote branches\ngit config --global fetch.prune true\n\n# Default push behavior\ngit config --global push.default current\ngit config --global push.autoSetupRemote true\n```\n\n### Useful Aliases\n\n```bash\n# Add to ~/.gitconfig\n[alias]\n    # Status shortcuts\n    st = status -sb\n\n    # Log formats\n    lg = log --oneline --graph --decorate -20\n    lga = log --oneline --graph --decorate --all -20\n\n    # Branch operations\n    co = checkout\n    cob = checkout -b\n    br = branch -vv\n    brd = branch -d\n\n    # Commit shortcuts\n    ci = commit\n    ca = commit --amend\n    can = commit --amend --no-edit\n\n    # Diff shortcuts\n    df = diff\n    dfs = diff --staged\n\n    # Undo operations\n    unstage = reset HEAD --\n    uncommit = reset --soft HEAD~1\n\n    # Show recent branches\n    recent = for-each-ref --sort=-committerdate refs/heads/ --format=''%(refname:short) - %(committerdate:relative)''\n\n    # Clean merged branches\n    cleanup = \"!git branch --merged | grep -v ''\\\\*\\\\|main\\\\|master\\\\|develop'' | xargs -n 1 git branch -d\"\n```\n\n## Common Operations\n\n### Undo Operations\n\n```bash\n# Undo last commit (keep changes staged)\ngit reset --soft HEAD~1\n\n# Undo last commit (keep changes unstaged)\ngit reset HEAD~1\n\n# Undo last commit (discard changes)\ngit reset --hard HEAD~1\n\n# Undo uncommitted changes to file\ngit checkout -- path/to/file\n\n# Undo staged changes\ngit reset HEAD path/to/file\n\n# Revert a pushed commit (creates new commit)\ngit revert <commit-sha>\n```\n\n### Stashing\n\n```bash\n# Stash current changes\ngit stash\n\n# Stash with message\ngit stash save \"WIP: feature description\"\n\n# Include untracked files\ngit stash -u\n\n# List stashes\ngit stash list\n\n# Apply most recent stash\ngit stash pop\n\n# Apply specific stash\ngit stash apply stash@{2}\n\n# Drop stash\ngit stash drop stash@{0}\n```\n\n### Cherry-Picking\n\n```bash\n# Apply single commit\ngit cherry-pick <commit-sha>\n\n# Apply multiple commits\ngit cherry-pick <sha1> <sha2> <sha3>\n\n# Apply range of commits\ngit cherry-pick <sha1>^..<sha2>\n\n# Cherry-pick without committing\ngit cherry-pick -n <commit-sha>\n```\n\n### Bisect (Find Bug Introduction)\n\n```bash\n# Start bisect\ngit bisect start\n\n# Mark current as bad\ngit bisect bad\n\n# Mark known good commit\ngit bisect good <commit-sha>\n\n# Git checks out middle commit; test and mark\ngit bisect good  # or bad\n\n# When done\ngit bisect reset\n```\n\n## Safety Guidelines\n\n### Never Do on Shared Branches\n\n```bash\n# NEVER force push to main/develop\ngit push --force origin main  # DANGEROUS\n\n# NEVER rebase public branches\ngit rebase main  # on shared feature branch\n\n# NEVER reset pushed commits\ngit reset --hard HEAD~3  # if already pushed\n```\n\n### Safe Alternatives\n\n```bash\n# Instead of force push, use:\ngit push --force-with-lease  # Fails if remote changed\n\n# Instead of rebase on shared branch, use:\ngit merge origin/main\n\n# Instead of reset pushed commits, use:\ngit revert <sha>\n```\n\n## Checklist\n\nBefore committing:\n- [ ] Changes are atomic (one logical change)\n- [ ] Commit message follows conventional format\n- [ ] Tests pass locally\n- [ ] No debug code or console.logs\n- [ ] No secrets or credentials\n- [ ] Branch is up to date with target\n\nBefore creating PR:\n- [ ] Rebased on latest main/develop\n- [ ] All commits have meaningful messages\n- [ ] PR is appropriately sized (< 400 lines)\n- [ ] Description explains what and why\n- [ ] Related issues are linked\n- [ ] CI checks pass\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Solution |\n|--------------|---------|----------|\n| `git add .` blindly | Commits unintended files | Use `git add -p` or specific files |\n| \"WIP\" commits | Unclear history | Squash before merge |\n| Force push to shared | Overwrites team work | Use `--force-with-lease` |\n| Long-lived branches | Merge conflicts | Keep branches < 1 week |\n| Large PRs | Slow reviews, bugs | Split into smaller PRs |\n| Merge commits locally | Messy history | Rebase for updates |\n| Ignoring CI failures | Broken main branch | Fix before merge |\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n- [Pro Git Book](https://git-scm.com/book/en/v2)\n- [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/)\n- [Git Flight Rules](https://github.com/k88hudson/git-flight-rules)\n- [Oh Shit, Git!?!](https://ohshitgit.com/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:00:19.966Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring streamlined Git workflows and collaboration tools.","zh":"适用于需要简化 Git 工作流和协作工具的开发代理。","ja":"Git ワークフローとコラボレーションツールを簡素化する必要がある開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Git 워크플ロー와 협업 도구를 간소화해야 하는 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollo que requieren flujos de trabajo de Git optimizados y herramientas de colaboración.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant des flux de travail Git rationalisés et des outils de collaboration.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungssagenten, die optimierte Git-Workflows und Kollaborationstools benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de fluxos de trabalho Git otimizados e ferramentas de colaboração.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, требующих оптимизированных рабочих процессов Git и инструментов сотрудничества.","ar":"مثالي لأعضاء الفريق الذين يحتاجون إلى عمليات عمل Git مبسطة وأدوات تعاون."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage complex projects using atomic commits, conventional commit formats, and clean history rebasing, while facilitating team collaboration through standardized branch naming and pull request management, all leveraging Git best practices and protocols.","zh":"使代理能够使用原子提交、传统提交格式和清洁历史重置来管理复杂项目，同时通过标准化分支命名和拉取请求管理来促进团队协作，所有这些都利用 Git 最佳实践和协议。","ja":"エージェントが、原子コミット、従来のコミット形式、クリーンな履歴のリベースを使用して複雑なプロジェクトを管理し、標準化されたブランチ命名とプルリクエスト管理を通じてチームコラボレーションを促進することを可能にし、すべて Git のベストプラクティスとプロトコルを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 원자 커밋, 전통적인 커밋 형식 및 깨끗한 기록 다시 설정을 사용하여 복잡한 프로젝트를 관리하고, 표준화된 브랜치命名 및 풀 요청 관리를 통해 팀 협력을 촉진하며, 모든 것을 Git의 모범 사례 및 프로토콜을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar proyectos complejos utilizando commits atómicos, formatos de commits convencionales y rebasado de historial limpio, mientras facilita la colaboración en equipo a través de la nominación de ramas estandarizadas y la gestión de solicitudes de extracción, todo aprovechando las mejores prácticas y protocolos de Git.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer des projets complexes en utilisant des commits atomiques, des formats de commit conventionnels et un rebasage d''historique propre, tout en facilitant la collaboration d''équipe grâce à la nomination de branches standardisées et à la gestion des demandes d''extraction, le tout en exploitant les meilleures pratiques et les protocoles Git.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, komplexe Projekte mithilfe von atomaren Commits, konventionellen Commit-Formaten und sauberem History-Rebasing zu verwalten, während die Teamzusammenarbeit durch standardisierte Branch-Namenskonventionen und Pull-Request-Management erleichtert wird, all dies unter Ausnutzung der Git-Best-Practices und -Protokolle.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar projetos complexos usando commits atômicos, formatos de commit convencionais e rebase de histórico limpo, ao mesmo tempo em que facilita a colaboração em equipe por meio de nomes de branch padronizados e gerenciamento de solicitações de pull, tudo aproveitando as melhores práticas e protocolos do Git.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять сложными проектами с помощью атомарных коммитов, конвенциональных форматов коммитов и чистого ребейза истории, а также облегчает командное сотрудничество посредством стандартизированных имен веток и управления запросами на слияние, все это при помощи лучших практик и протоколов Git.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إدارة مشاريع معقدة باستخدام الإلتزامات الذرية والتنسيقات التقليدية للإلتزامات وتحديث التاريخ النظيف، في حين تسهيل التعاون الفريقى من خلال أسماء الفرع المعيارية وإدارة طلبات السحب، كل ذلك بالاستفادة من أفضل الممارسات وبروتوكولات Git."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating commit validation using conventional commit formats","Resolving merge conflicts efficiently through clean history rebasing","Streamlining team collaboration with standardized branch naming conventions"],"zh":["使用传统提交格式自动验证提交","通过清洁历史重置高效地解决合并冲突","使用标准化分支命名约定简化团队协作"],"ja":["従来のコミット形式を使用してコミットの検証を自動化する","クリーンな履歴のリベースを通じてマージコンフリクトを効率的に解決する","標準化されたブランチ命名規約を使用してチームコラボレーションを簡素化する"],"ko":["전통적인 커밋 형식을 사용하여 커밋 유효성을 자동으로 검증","깨끗한 기록 다시 설정을 통해 병합 충돌을 효율적으로 해결","표준화된 브랜치命名 규칙을 사용하여 팀 협력을 간소화"],"es":["Automatizar la validación de commits utilizando formatos de commits convencionales","Resolver conflictos de fusiones de manera eficiente a través de rebasado de historial limpio","Optimizar la colaboración en equipo con convenciones de nominación de ramas estandarizadas"],"fr":["Automatiser la validation des commits en utilisant des formats de commit conventionnels","Résoudre les conflits de fusion de manière efficace grâce au rebasage d''historique propre","Rationaliser la collaboration d''équipe avec des conventions de nomination de branches standardisées"],"de":["Automatisieren der Commit-Validierung mithilfe konventioneller Commit-Formate","Effizientes Auflösen von Merge-Konflikten durch sauberes History-Rebasing","Optimieren der Teamzusammenarbeit mit standardisierten Branch-Namenskonventionen"],"pt":["Automatizar a validação de commit usando formatos de commit convencionais","Resolver conflitos de mesclagem de forma eficiente por meio de rebase de histórico limpo","Otimizar a colaboração em equipe com convenções de nomenclatura de branch padronizadas"],"ru":["Автоматизировать проверку коммитов с помощью конвенциональных форматов коммитов","Эффективно разрешать конфликты слияния посредством чистого ребейза истории","Оптимизировать командное сотрудничество с помощью стандартизированных имен веток"],"ar":["تأتمتة التحقق من الإلتزام باستخدام تنسيقات الإلتزام التقليدية","حَلّ النزاعات الناجمة عن دمج التحديثات بفعالية من خلال تحديث التاريخ النظيف","تحسين تعاون الفريق باستخدام أسماء الفرع المعيارية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git version control system","Limited to Git-based workflows and collaboration"],"zh":["需要 Git 版本控制系统","仅限于 Git 基础工作流和协作"],"ja":["Git バージョン管理システムが必要","Git ベースのワークフローとコラボレーションに限定される"],"ko":["Git 버전 관리 시스템이 필요","Git 기반 워크플ロー 및 협력에 한정"],"es":["Requiere sistema de control de versiones Git","Limitado a flujos de trabajo y colaboración basados en Git"],"fr":["Nécessite un système de contrôle de version Git","Limité aux flux de travail et à la collaboration basés sur Git"],"de":["Benötigt Git-versionskontrollsystem","Begrenzt auf Git-basierte Workflows und Kollaboration"],"pt":["Exige sistema de controle de versão Git","Limitado a fluxos de trabalho e colaboração baseados em Git"],"ru":["Требует системы контроля версий Git","Ограничен рабочими процессами и сотрудничеством на основе Git"],"ar":["يحتاج إلى نظام التحكم في الإصدار Git","محدود بالعمليات والتعاون المبني على Git"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"c184bb2e8655c48cea73192c13f521a387b10ddab5423a0b8d61a333e12391d5","qualityScore":60}');
